bridge/maestro.py is a Python port of parts of libmaestro from pbpctrl
(https://github.com/qzed/pbpctrl), Copyright (c) 2022 Maximilian Luz.
pbpctrl is dual-licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0; this port is used and
distributed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).
Ported material: the HDLC frame encoder/decoder and CRC usage
(libmaestro/src/hdlc), the pw_rpc 65599 name hash (src/pwrpc/id.rs), the
Maestro peer/channel address map and channel resolution
(src/protocol/addr.rs, src/protocol/utils.rs), the Maestro message field
numbers (proto/maestro_pw.proto) and the setting conversions, including the
balance encoding and the ANC cycle order (src/service/settings.rs,
cli/src/main.rs). Modifications: rewritten in Python, decoders made
byte-bounded and strict for untrusted input, and a blocking RPC client
written for this project. The protocol test vectors in
tests/python/test_maestro.py marked "(pbpctrl)" come from pbpctrl's unit
tests under the same license.

The pw_rpc packet field numbers follow the wire format defined by the
Pigweed project (https://pigweed.dev), The Pigweed Authors. Only that
interface reference data is used; no Pigweed code is included.

The connection approach (a client-role BlueZ Profile1 for the Maestro UUID,
then Device1.ConnectProfile) and the Pixel Buds Pro 2 device class constant
follow pbpctrl's cli/src/bt.rs.
